How to Choose Cotton Sanitary Pads for Heavy Flow

Heavy-flow days can require extra attention when choosing sanitary pads. If you prefer cotton sanitary pads, it is important to understand that the presence of cotton alone does not determine the absorbency of a product.

A sanitary pad is made using multiple layers, and each layer has a specific purpose. Depending on the product, cotton may be used in the top layer or other parts of the pad, while additional materials may contribute to absorption and leakage protection.

When selecting a cotton sanitary pad for heavier flow, start by considering absorbency. Choose an option designed to handle the amount of flow you normally experience. A suitable pad should provide enough coverage for your needs without making you feel uncomfortable.

Length is another important factor. A longer pad may offer additional coverage and can be particularly useful during heavier days. For overnight use, you may prefer a longer design that provides coverage while you move during sleep.

Fit is equally important. A sanitary pad that shifts during walking or daily activities can become uncomfortable. Wings can help secure the pad to underwear and keep it positioned properly.

You should also consider how frequently you need to change your pad. Even when using a high-absorbency product, it is important to change your menstrual product regularly according to your flow and comfort.

If your flow is consistently much heavier than usual, lasts unusually long or interferes with your everyday activities, consider speaking with a healthcare professional.

Cotton-based sanitary pads can be an option for people who prefer the feel of cotton. But when dealing with heavy flow, always look at the complete product—cotton material, absorbency, length, coverage and fit.

Understanding your own flow can make choosing the right sanitary pad much easier.

